OL,3,GNEWSAResidents in limbo two months
OL,4,Aafter roof collapse
OL,5,
OL,6,FAlmost two months after part of two
OL,7,Fhouses collapsed in south-east London,
OL,8,Fresidents say they remain in "a limbo
OL,9,Fof not knowing" over repairs, insurance
OL,10,Fclaims and when they can return home.
OL,12,FThe partial collapse happened on
OL,13,FWoodland Terrace in Charlton at about
OL,14,F18:30 BST on 22 August, when part of a
OL,15,Froof facade came down, affecting 14
OL,16,Fprivately owned properties, according
OL,17,Fto the council.
OL,19,FNo injuries were reported, but several
OL,20,Fproperties were evacuated and residents
OL,21,Fwere told they could not return until
OL,22,Fthe buildings had been declared safe.
OL,23,APub: 20-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,325,320,200,140,0,100
